**Technical Specification Document: Connected Devices and Smart Systems Integration**

**Project Title:** SmartHome 360 Integration  
**Version:** 1.3  
**Date:** October 15, 2023  
**Prepared by:** Tech Innovations Inc.  
**Contact:** Johnathan Smith, Lead Systems Engineer, js@techinnovations.com  

**1. Overview**  
The SmartHome 360 Integration project aims to enhance residential automation through the deployment of interconnected devices, sensors, and smart systems. This initiative will leverage the latest technologies from IoT Solutions Corp. and sensor hardware from SensorTech Ltd. to enable real-time data collection and analytics. 

**2. Requirements**  
- **Connected Devices:** All devices must support MQTT protocol for seamless communication. Devices include the SmartThermostat V2.0, SmartLight Pro, and SmartLock 3.1.  
- **Sensors:** Environmental sensors (temperature, humidity) from SensorTech Ltd. must be deployed throughout the residence, with a target of at least 10 units per home.  
- **Data Collection:** Data must be collected continuously and transmitted to the cloud-based platform on AWS (Amazon Web Services) using a secure API. Data retention must comply with GDPR regulations, with a maximum retention period of 24 months.  
- **Smart Systems:** Integration with Google Home and Amazon Alexa is mandatory to ensure voice control capabilities.

**3. Constraints**  
- **Network Limitation:** The system must operate on a minimum internet speed of 10 Mbps, as verified by SpeedTest Pro.  
- **Power Consumption:** All devices must operate on low power (max 5W) to ensure compatibility with solar energy systems, particularly in eco-friendly constructions in California.  
- **User Privacy:** All data must be anonymized before storage to protect user privacy, complying with CCPA guidelines.  

**4. Dependencies**  
- The project depends on timely delivery of the SmartThermostat V2.0 from EcoSmart Devices, scheduled for November 10, 2023.  
- Collaboration with Data Insights Group for analytics framework is crucial, targeting a prototype by December 1, 2023.  
- Testing phase will involve partnerships with 20 households in Austin, Texas, to validate system performance and user experience by January 15, 2024.

